&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div&gt;PhysicsX is a deep-tech company with roots in numerical physics and Formula One, dedicated to accelerating hardware innovation at the speed of software.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We are building an AI-driven simulation software stack for engineering and manufacturing across advanced industries. By enabling high-fidelity, multi-physics simulation through AI inference across the entire engineering lifecycle, PhysicsX unlocks new levels of optimization and automation in design, manufacturing, and operations — empowering engineers to push the boundaries of possibility. Our customers include leading innovators in Aerospace &amp;amp; Defense, Materials, Energy, Semiconductors, and Automotive.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PhysicsX is looking for a Senior Financial Accountant to join our growing finance team. This is a technically demanding role for a qualified accountant who is confident working across complex, multi-entity, multi-jurisdiction accounting — and who wants to take genuine ownership of the processes they run.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be a key part of a team of four, reporting directly to the Finance Manager, and acting as the point of contact for group tax and statutory reporting across our UK, US, and Singapore entities. You&#39;ll work closely with external tax consultants, auditors, and advisers, and be expected to take clear ownership of the workstreams you lead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone who thrives on responsibility, brings fresh thinking to improve processes and controls, and has the technical depth to navigate regulatory complexity across multiple jurisdictions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Revenue recognition&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading global revenue recognition in line with FRS 102, ensuring accuracy and consistency with Group accounting policies across all entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tax compliance and advisory&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting group tax compliance across the UK, US, and Singapore — acting as the main point of contact between the business and our external tax advisers, and helping to ensure corporation tax returns and year-end filings, including federal, state, and local obligations, are completed accurately and on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing VAT and GST compliance obligations across jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting R&amp;amp;D tax credit claims in collaboration with specialist advisers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accounts receivable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the AR function end-to-end — including customer invoicing, cash allocation, and credit control — ensuring timely and accurate processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Accounting &amp;amp; Standards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining compliance with complex accounting standards across the group, including lease accounting (IFRS 16) and share-based payments (IFRS 2).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assessing and implementing new or amended standards as they come into effect, ensuring Group accounting policies remain current and consistent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acting as the internal point of reference for technical accounting queries across the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Statutory and regulatory reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading timely and accurate statutory and regulatory reporting across the group, ensuring compliance with IFRS, UK GAAP, and relevant local standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing audit support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Controls and process improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building and evolving a robust but agile financial controls framework — strong enough for scale and audit-readiness, without slowing the business down.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with the wider organisation to embed smarter financial processes, helping teams understand and adopt improved ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying and implementing process improvements to strengthen controls, efficiency, and reporting quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes a Great Candidate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A qualified accountant (ACA or ACCA) with at least four to five years of relevant post-qualification experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical accounting knowledge — you&#39;re confident with IFRS, UK GAAP, and comfortable navigating multi-jurisdiction regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience across tax compliance, revenue recognition, and statutory reporting — you&#39;ll be expected to bring technical confidence to these areas from day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a technology, engineering, SaaS or high-growth start-up environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accurate and detail-oriented — you take pride in getting things right and spot inconsistencies others might miss.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to own and execute workstreams independently, while working collaboratively as part of a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organisational and time management skills — you prioritise effectively, manage competing demands, and consistently deliver to deadline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive communicator — with both internal stakeholders and external advisers — who flags issues early and knows when to escalate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in a fast-moving, high-growth environment where the landscape is constantly evolving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contract: Permanent, full-time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: London - hybrid, with 3 days per week in the office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reports to: Finance Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build what actually matters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help shape an AI-native engineering company at a formative stage, tackling problems that genuinely matter for industry and society. This is work with real-world impact - and something you can be proud to stand behind.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn alongside exceptional people&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work with a high-caliber, collaborative team of engineers, scientists, and operators who care deeply about doing great work, and about helping each other get better. We come from diverse backgrounds, but we share a commitment to operating at the highest level and addressing some of the most complex challenges out there. If you’re ambitious, thoughtful, and driven by impact, you’ll feel at home.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence over hierarchy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate with a flat structure: good ideas win&amp;nbsp;- wherever they come from. Questioning assumptions and challenging the status quo isn’t just welcomed, it’s expected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sustainable pace, long-term ambition&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Building meaningful technology is a marathon, not a sprint. We believe in balancing focused, ambitious work with a life beyond it. Our hybrid model blends time together in our Shoreditch office with work-from-home days, giving you the flexibility to work sustainably while staying connected in person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And it doesn’t stop there …&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚀&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Equity options&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- share meaningfully in the company you’re helping to build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏦&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;10% employer pension contribution&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- because investing in future matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍽️&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Free office lunches&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- to keep you energised and focused.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👶&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Enhanced parental leave&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- 3 months full pay paternity and 6 months full pay maternity leave, to provide extra flexibility during the moments that matter most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍼&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;YellowNest nursery scheme&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- to help working parents manage childcare costs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;☀️&amp;nbsp;25 days of Annual Leave (+ Public Holidays)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;- because taking time to rest matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏥&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Private medical insurance&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- 100% employee cover, giving you complete peace of mind.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💪&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Wellhub Subscription&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;- gain access to thousands of gyms, classes and wellness apps, supporting both physical and mental wellbeing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👀&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Eye tests&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- because good work depends on good health.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📈&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Personal development&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- dedicated support for learning, development, and leveling up over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💛&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Assistance Programme (EAP)&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- confidential wellbeing support, available whenever you need it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚲&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Bike2Work scheme and&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;🚆&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Season ticket loan&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- to make getting to work easier and greener.&lt;/p&gt;
